00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:20.140
And so they've gone to court trying

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.274
to force

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:22.809
the president to be found in contempt.

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:24.277
And so far,

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:25.178
they still believe

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.946
documents are have led to have yet

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.014
to be returned.

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:28.381
The former

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:29.249
president says

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:30.383
that he doesn't have anything,

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:32.519
anything left in his possession Anderson.

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:33.553
Evan Perez, appreciate it.

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:34.120
Conservative lawyer

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.455
George Conway joins us now.

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:36.256
He's also contributing

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:37.857
columnist The Washington Post and joining

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:38.791
us, as well as former Maine

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.426
Republican Senator William Cohen,

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:41.628
who served as defense secretary

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:43.229
during the Clinton administration.

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:43.796
So, George,

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:44.797
we're talking about a document

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:45.598
containing information

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.333
about a potential attack on Iran.

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.902
We obviously have not seen this document.

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:51.271
We don't know exactly the nature of it.

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:53.006
How concerning is it, though,

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:54.774
that these attorneys say

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.242
they're unable to find it?

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.244
Well, it is concerning that the document

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.913
was apparently flying around

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:02.982
from Washington to Mar a Lago, perhaps,

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:04.050
and then to Bedminster.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.785
But I think at the end of the day,

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.687
in terms of a potential prosecution, it's

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:08.621
not going to matter.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:09.789
What matters is the fact

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:10.423
that he is

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:12.058
said to have acknowledged

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:14.394
President Trump on this tape,

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:16.963
that he possessed classified documents

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:18.831
and that he knew he possessed

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.733
classified documents and the fact

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.569
he that that was his state of mind

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:23.736
when he was requested

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:24.871
to have the documents

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:27.106
back later in the next year

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.342
and then refused to give them back

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.510
and then gave some of them back

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.312
and then lied about giving them all back

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:33.413
and so on and so forth.

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:33.713
I mean, it's

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:35.815
just another smoking gun

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:37.850
in a smoking arsenal.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:38.918
Secretary Cohen, again,

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:39.786
we don't know

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:41.854
what this exact document was.

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:43.823
Would there be other copies of it

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:47.560
that prosecutors would have access to

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.829
or would they be able to reach out

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:50.163
to somebody

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:50.730
in the Pentagon

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.264
to find out

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:53.666
exactly what this document may have been?

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:55.568
Well, if the document did exist

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:56.703
and certainly

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.771
the Pentagon would have access to it,

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.574
if the former president is quoting

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:03.743
something about Chairman Milley,

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:04.410
then Chairman

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.280
Milley obviously would be a source

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:10.216
to go to to say what was it,

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:11.084
what was involved?

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:12.218
But rather than look

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:13.886
at the legal side of it, George

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:15.321
can certainly do that.

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.055
I'd like to talk

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:16.723
a little bit

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:17.857
about the implications

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:19.826
for our national security.

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:21.294
We spend billions,

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:22.762
tens of billions of dollars

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:24.297
collecting intelligence in order

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:26.132
to protect the American people.

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:27.033
The notion

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:29.135
that we are so cavalier,

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:30.370
our elected leaders,

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.471
the president of United States,

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:34.207
is so cavalier about those documents

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.510
puts our men and women in grave danger.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.245
And just today in The Washington Post,

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:41.080
there's an article, lead article

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.249
talking about Iran planning to help

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.985
kill American soldiers in Syria

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:48.588
at the behest of the Russians.

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:50.723
So this is what's involved to say,

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:52.892
why are we making a big deal about this?

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:55.228
Because lives really are at stake.

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:56.963
Our men and women are serving

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:57.630
as are at stake,

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.198
and the American people's security

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:00.333
is compromised

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:02.101
when this kind of information gets out.

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:02.402
George,

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:03.469
the former president was asked

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:04.470
about the document

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.572
and this recording of him acknowledging

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:07.974
he had classified documents.

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:09.475
Here's what he told Fox.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:11.978
I don't know anything about it.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:12.545
All I know is,

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:14.681
is everything I did was right.

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:16.749
We have the Presidential Records Act,

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:19.786
which I abided by 100%.

00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:20.586
I mean, obviously, it's

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:21.888
a ludicrous answer.

00:05:21.888 --> 00:05:22.555
I'm just saying

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:23.656
he doesn't know anything about it.

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:25.158
There's allegedly

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:27.393
a recording of his voice on this.

00:05:27.427 --> 00:05:28.161
He could easily

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:29.796
look at his or ask

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:30.630
somebody about it

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.165
if you wanted to answer that question.

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:34.300
How does all of this complicate

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.401
the former president's defense

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:35.835
as it relates

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.837
